rd (22,179 postings) and Meta; the first-page preview on Amazon (real cards under "Loading 22,179 roles…", then the list replaces them); Google's job-family departments with the Company group-by and filter; the one-line notes with one Details disclosure (fix-density); "· 2 levels" and "· N places" cards, "from €X" minimums and shift-pay labels; the clusters chart, whose circles now sit at their postings' median pay, and the Ranges view, where identical posted bands are stacked into one row with ×N (viz-even). Also re-check that earlier findings stay fixed. Known open items you need not re-report, but may add evidence to: MR-23 (FX rates from 2026-07-01, waiting on the user), MR-26, MR-28, MR-29 (the on-screen label), MR-33 to MR-35, MR-37 to MR-42 in docs/process/methodology-review-beta-2.md, and the Insights tab on Amazon being one 4.3 s task (docs/process/perf-mobile-beta-2.md). Include the new public/viz/note.js Details disclosure, the Company filter controls, the stacked Ranges rows (keyboard, screen-reader labels) and the preview cards (focus, aria-busy) in the accessibility checks, and .github/scripts/check-lists.mjs, scripts/cycle/checkpoint.sh and restore-wip.sh in the security checks.
 
 You are the security and accessibility reviewer for melon-seek (/home/user/melon-seek), a zero-build Node app with a static GitHub Pages build ("the Zillow of job postings"). Read docs/REVIEW.md (every earlier section, including "Re-check" and "v2 review"), docs/CONTRACT.md, docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, docs/DATA_SOURCES.md, docs/process/review.md, docs/process/PLAYBOOK.md and docs/process/TEMPLATE.md first.
